WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.461
On most blockchains,

00:00:01.461 --> 00:00:03.339
anyone who knows an address can read its

00:00:03.339 --> 00:00:05.643
balance and every amount it paid.

00:00:05.643 --> 00:00:08.774
On Aztec, each token has two balances.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:10.583
Nulo handles both for you.

00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:11.974
Your private balance:

00:00:11.974 --> 00:00:13.574
only you can see it.

00:00:13.574 --> 00:00:15.000
Your public balance:

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.009
anyone can see it,

00:00:16.009 --> 00:00:17.904
like a balance on Ethereum.

00:00:17.904 --> 00:00:19.157
Your private balance is a

00:00:19.157 --> 00:00:20.513
set of encrypted notes,

00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:22.600
like cash in sealed envelopes.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.165
The network keeps a fingerprint

00:00:24.165 --> 00:00:25.081
of each note,

00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:27.948
and a sealed copy only its owner can open.

00:00:27.948 --> 00:00:30.522
Say you pay 3.50 from a note worth 5.

00:00:30.522 --> 00:00:33.791
Nulo spends that note and makes new ones:

00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:35.600
3.50 for the person you pay,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.687
and 1.50 change for you.

00:00:37.687 --> 00:00:38.904
In a private payment,

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:41.235
the record shows that something was spent.

00:00:41.235 --> 00:00:42.974
It does not show which note,

00:00:42.974 --> 00:00:44.278
or how much.

00:00:44.278 --> 00:00:45.600
Moving money to your public

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.898
balance is your choice,

00:00:46.898 --> 00:00:49.078
and the public side records the amount.

00:00:49.078 --> 00:00:50.678
Nulo labels each balance,

00:00:50.678 --> 00:00:52.557
so you always know which is which.
